+# `archive/gem_standalone/` — the standalone Candida etcGEM, retired
+
+**This code is no longer maintained here. The model it implements now lives in
+[`GabYvonDurocher/etcGEMs`](https://github.com/GabYvonDurocher/etcGEMs), where the four
+*Candida* species are strains on the shared core.**
+
+This directory is kept **as it stood**, unmodified, so that every number in the manuscript
+can still be traced to the script that produced it. Nothing in it should be developed
+further; changes to the model belong in `etcGEMs`.
+
+## Why it was retired
+
+`gem/` was a second implementation of the enzyme- and temperature-constrained GEM: its own
+enzyme-cost layer, its own thermal function, its own path map, species handled by a
+dictionary rather than by folders. The rule the group adopted for the O2 model applies —
+the method lives in one place and does not drift between implementations — so the four
+species became `strains/` entries in `etcGEMs`, and this became the record rather than the
+tool.
+
+## The port is verified, not asserted
+
+`etcGEMs` reproduces this implementation's locked numbers, at a stated tolerance, with the
+comparison run as a script that exits non-zero if it ever stops holding:
+`reports/candida_thermal_limit/gate_table.py` — **79 of 79 comparisons pass**, the fitted
+globals to every digit stored in `tables/etcgem_calib.json`, and all 48 predicted growth
+rates exactly. The expected values are frozen in a committed fixture
+(`reports/candida_thermal_limit/standalone_expected.json`) carrying this repository's commit
+hash and the md5 of each source file, so the check keeps working with this directory
+archived and needs no copy of this repository.
+
+Full record: `reports/candida_thermal_limit/K1_port_verification.md` in `etcGEMs`.
+
+## What changed in the port, and what did not
+
+Nothing scientific changed at K1: the port was configured to match this implementation and
+the gate is the proof. Two findings about this code came out of the porting, both recorded
+in the K1 report and both since acted on in `etcGEMs`:
+
+* `ATP_Maintenance__cyto` ships **reversible** in iDC1003, so the solver ran maintenance
+  backwards and *C. parapsilosis* collected free ATP. `19_etcgem_counterfactual.py` and
+  `22_thermal_sensitivity.py` here already correct it; `18_build_etcgem_tpc.py` does not, and
+  the locked µ table comes from 18. `etcGEMs` makes the correction the default and keeps the
+  uncorrected run as a labelled sensitivity.
+* `15_run_seq2tm.py` truncates sequences at 1022 aa, citing an ESM-2 positional limit that
+  does not exist (ESM-2 uses rotary position embeddings). The committed
+  `tables/thermal_tm.csv` was produced **without** truncation, so the script as it stands
+  does not reproduce the table beside it — by up to 2.6 °C on affected batches.
+
+K2 then put the four species on the shared thermal form and K3 retired this directory. What
+moved between K1 and K2, and why, is in `reports/candida_thermal_limit/K2_core_thermal_form.md`.
+
+## If you need an etcGEM output
+
+Take it from a **pinned commit of `etcGEMs`, by path** — never vendor it back here. The
+strains are `strains/{cauris_iRV973,chaemulonii_draft,cduobushaemulonii_draft,cparapsilosis_iDC1003}/`
+and their outputs are under each strain's `outputs/`, with the cross-strain summaries in
+`outputs/transfer_*/`.
+
+## What still reads this directory
+
+`scripts/19_fig4.R` draws Figure 4 from `tables/` here, and `scripts/run_all.sh` can
+regenerate those tables with `RUN_GEM=1`. Both were repointed when this directory moved.
+Every script here resolves its own paths from its own location (`gempaths.py`), so the move
+required no change inside it.
